Here's a complete multi-step JCL job to create, populate, and verify a VSAM KSDS:

```jcl
//VSAMJOB  JOB (ACCT,DEPT),'VSAM KSDS COMPLETE',
//         CLASS=A,MSGCLASS=X,NOTIFY=&SYSUID,COND=(0,NE)
//*
//* STEP 1: DELETE EXISTING KSDS IF IT EXISTS
//*
//DELETE   EXEC PGM=IDCAMS
//SYSPRINT DD SYSOUT=*
//SYSIN    DD *
  DELETE PROD.CUSTOMER.KSDS CLUSTER PURGE
  IF LASTCC NE 0 THEN SET MAXCC = 0
/*
//*
//* STEP 2: DEFINE NEW VSAM KSDS CLUSTER
//*
//DEFINE   EXEC PGM=IDCAMS
//SYSPRINT DD SYSOUT=*
//SYSIN    DD *
  DEFINE CLUSTER -
    (NAME(PROD.CUSTOMER.KSDS) -
     INDEXED -
     KEYS(6 0) -
     RECORDSIZE(500 500) -
     SHAREOPTIONS(2 3) -
     TRACKS -
     CYLINDERS(100 20) -
     RECORDSPERCI(20) -
     VOLUMES(DISK01 DISK02)) -
  DATA -
    (NAME(PROD.CUSTOMER.KSDS.DATA) -
     CONTROLINTERVAL(4096) -
     BUFFERSPACE(24576)) -
  INDEX -
    (NAME(PROD.CUSTOMER.KSDS.INDEX) -
     CONTROLINTERVAL(2048))
/*
//*
//* STEP 3: REPRO FROM SEQUENTIAL FILE TO KSDS
//* Input file contains 500-byte records with key in first 6 bytes
//*
//LOAD     EXEC PGM=IDCAMS
//SYSPRINT DD SYSOUT=*
//INSEQ    DD DSN=PROD.CUSTOMER.UNLOAD,DISP=SHR,
//         VOL=SER=TAPE01,UNIT=TAPE
//OUTVSAM  DD DSN=PROD.CUSTOMER.KSDS,DISP=SHR
//SYSIN    DD *
  REPRO INFILE(INSEQ) OUTFILE(OUTVSAM) -
        REUSE
/*
//*
//* STEP 4: VERIFY CLUSTER WAS CREATED SUCCESSFULLY
//*
//LISTCAT  EXEC PGM=IDCAMS
//SYSPRINT DD SYSOUT=*
//SYSIN    DD *
  LISTCAT ENTRIES(PROD.CUSTOMER.KSDS) ALL
/*
//*
//* STEP 5: BUILD ALTERNATE INDEX ON CUSTOMER NAME
//*
//ALTIDX   EXEC PGM=IDCAMS
//SYSPRINT DD SYSOUT=*
//SYSIN    DD *
  DEFINE ALTERNATEINDEX -
    (NAME(PROD.CUSTOMER.KSDS.BYNAME) -
     RELATE(PROD.CUSTOMER.KSDS) -
     KEYS(30 6) -
     NONUNIQUEKEY -
     CYLINDERS(20 5)) -
  DATA -
    (NAME(PROD.CUSTOMER.KSDS.BYNAME.DATA)) -
  INDEX -
    (NAME(PROD.CUSTOMER.KSDS.BYNAME.INDEX))
/*
//*
//* STEP 6: POPULATE ALTERNATE INDEX
//*
//BLDIDX   EXEC PGM=IDCAMS
//SYSPRINT DD SYSOUT=*
//INFILE   DD DSN=PROD.CUSTOMER.KSDS,DISP=SHR
//OUTFILE  DD DSN=PROD.CUSTOMER.KSDS.BYNAME,DISP=SHR
//SYSIN    DD *
  BLDINDEX INFILE(INFILE) OUTFILE(OUTFILE)
/*
//*
//* STEP 7: DEFINE PATH TO ALTERNATE INDEX
//*
//DEFPATH  EXEC PGM=IDCAMS
//SYSPRINT DD SYSOUT=*
//SYSIN    DD *
  DEFINE PATH -
    (NAME(PROD.CUSTOMER.KSDS.BYNAME.PATH) -
     PATHENTRY(PROD.CUSTOMER.KSDS.BYNAME) -
     UPDATE)
/*
//*
//* STEP 8: VERIFY FINAL CATALOG ENTRIES
//*
//VERIFY   EXEC PGM=IDCAMS
//SYSPRINT DD SYSOUT=*
//SYSIN    DD *
  LISTCAT ENTRIES(PROD.CUSTOMER.**) ALL
/*
```

Job Flow Explanation:

**STEP 1 (DELETE)**: Removes previous version if exists (PURGE deletes all generations)

**STEP 2 (DEFINE)**: Creates KSDS cluster with:
- 6-byte key at position 0 (customer ID)
- Fixed 500-byte records
- SHAREOPTIONS(2 3) for concurrent read/write with locking
- 100 cylinders primary, 20 secondary allocation
- Separate DATA and INDEX components for performance

**STEP 3 (LOAD)**: Loads sequential file into KSDS
- Input records must be sorted by key
- REUSE option prevents duplicate key errors

**STEP 4 (LISTCAT)**: Verifies cluster creation
- Shows all cluster attributes
- Confirms record counts

**STEP 5-6 (ALTIDX)**: Creates secondary index on customer name
- Non-unique key (multiple customers per name)
- 30-byte key at position 6 in record

**STEP 7 (DEFPATH)**: Makes alternate index accessible by name

**STEP 8 (VERIFY)**: Final confirmation of all catalog entries

Error Handling: COND=(0,NE) aborts on any non-zero return code; individual STEPs reset MAXCC with IF LASTCC clauses.
